Package: gitu
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 git,
Description: terminal user interface for git, in the style of Magit
 gitu presents the working tree as a single buffer -- unstaged and staged
 changes, recent commits, stashes -- and acts on whatever the cursor is over,
 down to staging an individual hunk or line. Keybindings follow Magit's rather
 than git's subcommand names.
 .
 It reads repository state through libgit2 and shells out to git for the
 operations that write, so the git it drives is the one on PATH and behaves as
 configured.
